hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1614","Narrated to us Bundār, narrated to us Yaḥyā, on the authority of Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, who said: My father narrated to me, on the authority of ʿĀʾishah (RA), that the people entered upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he was ill, so he led them in prayer sitting, while they prayed standing. He gestured to them to sit and said:\n\n*\Indeed"","" the imam is only followed. So if he prays sitting"","" pray sitting; and if he prays standing"","" pray standing. If he bows"","" bow; if he prostrates"","" prostrate; and if he rises"","" rise.\""*\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""""
